nd cannot stand him in equal  measure on the one hand he's easy to  empathize with because he's one of the  more regular human characters in the  series being thrust into situations that  he is clearly not mentally prepared for  we've all been there but at the same  time calm yo farm his gags are genuinely  funny for the first couple of times but  the problem is especially in the first  few episodes he was in he just never  stops he screams and screams and screams  and screams and screams and then takes a  break to yell but after that he screams  and screams and screams and then he'll  do something cool and to be fair when he  is in actions any to is an absolute  highlight of the series I loved the idea  that he can only perform one technique  and the whole concept of just mastering  one thing in general and it just looks  so spectacular  every time he performs it also he has a  lot of decent dramatic substance in his  backstory and his struggle to get  through life but my god do we have to  sift through a lot of screaming and  being a general pervert to get there his  sustained energy is just a bit too much  for me although to be fair this did get  better over the course of the series and  I feel like he ended up as a much more  balanced character by the end then  there's also in ask and I thought I was  going to have the same problem with him  at first because for an episode or two  all he did was yell and yell about  wanting to fight but he got over that  really quickly and became a truly great  and enjoyable character he's good  all-rounder really is he can do some  great comedy some phenomenal action with  his amazing self-taught breathing and he  has a really super solid character  design always a feast for the eyes and a  charm for the mind and of course most of  the tertiary cast also falls into that  category there were very few characters  who were introduced in demon slayer that  I just plain did not like and actually I  can't think of any off the top of 