battle series my favourite twist of  which actually is the power system which  seems based almost entirely upon  breathing it's such a wonderful  representation of what focus and correct  technique can do to add potency impact  and mastery over a martial art it's not  an easy system to sell though and I  actually imagine that the manga has a  much more difficult time with this idea  but as a result of that difficulty it is  able to hit that much harder it's not as  simple as a magical powers acquiring a  quirk building and molding energy or  even consuming a devil fruit it's much  more basic than that and yet infinitely  more complicated and I just love the  idea that in theory any human in this  world could learn the techniques we see  on display in the series purely through  mastery of breath it's not restrictive  however as a result it accepts only the  very best with brutal consequences for  those deemed unworthy so it is a pure  triumph in that regard however with that  said demon sight does occasionally fall  into some Shonen traps one of which  occurred right at the tail end of the  anime when all of the hashira were  introduced together now some people may  not consider this a trap but in my  experience it's never a great idea to  introduce a large group of profound  characters all at once firstly because  the bombardment of characters lost a  great condensed experience for the  viewer or reader at the time doesn't  really allow for individuals to get the  attention they most certainly deserve  given their position and secondly  because it removes a huge layer of  intrigue going forward in the series so  for example I really loved when I only  knew of the existence of - huh sure  not knowing how many of them existed nor  what sort of crazy powers or designs  they inhabited gave a nice air of  mystery and made me want to explore this  bolt infinitely to discover all of them  so it was slightly disappointing to have  them all dumped on me all at once but  this is such a minor complaint as is  every negative aspect I've brought up in  this review none of the things I've  mentioned are series Breaking and for a  lot of people this might even be another  selling feature a ton of people might  love Zenit to stupidly high energy as  well as being embodied by high-level  characters and that's great it's just  not my personal preference but even with  those things in mind there is no way  that I can come away from this anime  with anything less than a glowing  recommendation I'm thrilled to have been  on board with this journey even if I did  jump on a fair bit light so as a result  it's been a fairly intense and condensed  experience but something that has  reminded me of why I loved the anime  medium and that pretty much does it for  my final thoughts on demon slayer if you  enjoyed this video and the content this  channel produced in general and please  do consider donating to the new ultra  view patreon because the support of all  of your amazing people is what continues  to make this channel possible and if  patreon isn't quite your style then  please do leave this video a like share  or subscribe because it also helps spot  this channel an incredible amount and if  you'd like to join the fun and anytime  and please do head over to my discord  server where a wide array of shenanigan  reign takes place on a daily basis and  finally please do comment with your  thoughts on Demon Slayer this has been  the new volt review and I'll see you  next time  [Music]

